ul.li:
configuration management systems that hold the desired state and
        perform deployments, often on endpoints that the monitoring system
        cannot reach;

section.t:
The information model is intended to be bound to other transports in
      the future, including a YANG data model and an SNMP notification profile;
      see .

section.sourcecode:
cert-observation-set = { version: 1, records: [+ cert-observation-record] }
cert-observation-record = { version: 1, ? record-id: tstr, reporter: tstr, subject: subject, location: location, evidence: evidence-type, observed-at: timestamp, ? valid-for: uint, ? certificate: certificate-info, ? chain: chain-info, ? expected-sha256: fingerprint, ? renewal-window: renewal-window, ? status: [+ status-value], ? extensions: { * tstr => any } }
subject = { ? host: tstr, ? service: tstr, ? id: tstr }
location = { ? address: tstr, ? port: uint .le 65535, ? sni: tstr, ? path: tstr, ? store: tstr, ? label: tstr, ? config-item: tstr }
evidence-type = "issued" / "declared" / "deployed" / "observed-store" / "observed-wire" / tstr
certificate-info = { sha256: fingerprint, ? subject-dn: tstr, ? san: [* tstr], ? issuer-dn: tstr, ? serial: tstr, ? not-before: timestamp, not-after: timestamp, ? public-key-algorithm: tstr, ? public-key-size: uint, ? signature-algorithm: tstr, ? der: tstr }
chain-info = { ? certificates: [* fingerprint], validation: "valid" / "invalid" / "incomplete" / "not-checked", ? trust-anchor: tstr }
renewal-window = { start: timestamp, end: timestamp }
status-value = "not-found" / "expired" / "not-yet-valid" / "chain-invalid" / "name-mismatch" / "unexpected-certificate" / tstr
timestamp = tstr ; RFC 3339 date-time, UTC fingerprint = tstr .regexp "[0-9a-f]{64}"

ul.li:
401 (Unauthorized) or 403 (Forbidden) when the Reporter is not
          authenticated, or is not authorised to report on one or more of the
          Subjects in the set ();

a "deployed" or "observed-store" fingerprint that differs from
          the "observed-wire" fingerprint: the service did not load the new
          certificate;

different "observed-wire" fingerprints for the same service name
          from different addresses: inconsistent nodes behind a load
          balancer;

a mapping to SNMP for devices that only support SNMP, including
        notifications for conditions such as a changed fingerprint or a
        certificate approaching expiry;
